Fuel Injection Equipment

@ Fuel oil system

The figure below shows the fuel oil system.

The fuel injection pumps are Yanmar YPE type.

The feed pump sucks up fuel oil from the fuel tank and feeds the oil to the fuel filter at a pressure of approximately
0.4 - 0.7 MPa.

The filtered fuel oil is sent to the pump and is pressurized by the plunger.

The fuel oil then flows through the injection pipe and injector and is injected from the nozzle to each cylinder.

